.Dd July 31, 2026
.Dt RACOONCTL 8
.Os
.\"
.Sh NAME
.Nm racoonctl
.Nd control and query a running racoon IKE daemon
.\"
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl dl
.Op Fl s Ar socket
.Ar command
.Op Ar args ...
.\"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is the tool for operating a running
.Xr racoon 8 :
establishing and tearing down VPN connections, inspecting the current
Security Associations and scheduled events, and reloading the daemon's
configuration.
It is the only supported way to do any of this at runtime;
.Xr racoon 8
itself only reads
.Xr racoon.conf 5
at startup or on
.Dv SIGHUP .
.Pp
With privilege separation
.Pq Ic privsep
active in
.Xr racoon.conf 5 ,
which is this project's recommended default (see the Admin Guide's
Privilege Separation section), racoon itself no longer runs as a single
root process an operator might otherwise reach for directly:
.Nm
talking to the admin socket is the intended, and only, interface for a
non-root operator to drive it.
.Pp
.Nm
talks to
.Xr racoon 8
over a
.Xr unix 4
domain socket (the
.Dq admin socket ,
sometimes called the adminport), configured by the
.Ic adminsock
directive in the
.Ic listen
block of
.Xr racoon.conf 5 .
By default that socket is owned
.Li root:root
mode
.Li 0600 ,
which only root can use.
For any non-root user to run
.Nm ,
three things must all be true:
.Bl -bullet
.It
.Xr racoon.conf 5 Ap s
.Ic listen
block has an active
.Ic adminsock
directive naming a group that user belongs to, e.g.
.Bd -literal -offset indent
adminsock "/var/run/racoon/racoon.sock" "root" "racoon" 0660;
.Ed
.Pp
(both packaged roadwarrior client/server examples ship this active by
default; see
.Pa examples/roadwarrior/ Ns Ar role Ns Pa /racoon.conf
under this project's documentation examples directory).
.It
the directory holding that socket (by default the
.Xr racoon 8
runtime state directory, e.g.
.Pa /run/racoon )
grants that same group traversal access.
Under systemd this is
.Ic RuntimeDirectoryMode=
in the shipped
.Pa racoon.service
unit; starting
.Xr racoon 8
manually instead requires creating that directory by hand at the same
group and mode first.
.It
the user is actually a member of that group.
.El
.Pp
See the Admin Guide's Privilege Separation section for the full
filesystem ownership policy this implies, and
.Xr racoon.conf 5 Ap s
.Sx Privilege separation
section for the
.Ic adminsock
directive's full syntax.
.Pp
The following general options are available:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl d
Debug mode.
Hexdump admin port messages before sending them.
.It Fl l
Increase verbosity.
Mainly affects
.Ic show-sa .
.It Fl s Ar socket
Connect to
.Ar socket
instead of the compile-time default (see
.Sx FILES
below).
Use this when the admin socket has been moved via
.Ic adminsock
in
.Xr racoon.conf 5 ,
or when driving more than one
.Xr racoon 8
instance from the same host.
.El
.\"
.Pp
The following commands are available:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ic reload-config
Tell
.Xr racoon 8
to reload
.Xr racoon.conf 5 ,
equivalent to sending it
.Dv SIGHUP .
Note that under privsep, changes to the
.Ic listen
and
.Ic paths
sections are not picked up by a reload; those require a full restart
(see
.Xr racoon.conf 5 Ap s
.Sx Privilege separation
section).
.It Ic show-schedule
Dump
.Xr racoon 8 Ap s
internal event scheduler queue: pending timer-driven work such as
rekeys, retransmissions, and DPD probes.
Primarily a debugging aid, not something a routine VPN operator needs.
.It Ic show-sa Op Ar protocol
Dump the current Security Associations: all of them if
.Ar protocol
is omitted, or only
.Ic isakmp
(Phase 1),
.Ic esp ,
.Ic ah ,
or
.Ic ipsec
(both ESP and AH) if given.
Use
.Fl l
for more detail per SA.
.It Ic get-cert Oo Ic inet | inet6 Oc Ar src dst
Output the raw certificate that authenticated the Phase 1 SA between
.Ar src
and
.Ar dst .
.It Ic flush-sa Op Ar protocol
Tear down all Security Associations, filtered the same way as
.Ic show-sa .
.It Ic delete-sa Ar saopts
Delete one specific Security Association; see
.Sx Parameter specifications
below for
.Ar saopts .
.It Ic establish-sa Oo Fl w Oc Oo Fl n Ar remoteconf Oc \
Oo Fl u Ar identity Oc Ar saopts
Establish one specific Security Association.
.Fl u Ar identity
supplies the XAuth/Hybrid-auth identity when the matching
.Ic remote
block requires one \(em
.Nm
prompts for the associated password interactively.
.Fl n Ar remoteconf
picks a specific
.Ic remote
block by name when more than one could match.
.Fl w
blocks until the SA is actually established (or fails), instead of
returning as soon as the request is sent.
.It Ic vpn-connect Oo Fl u Ar identity Oc Ar vpn_gateway
Shorthand for
.Ic establish-sa
that establishes an ISAKMP (Phase 1) SA with
.Ar vpn_gateway .
This is the command a roadwarrior client operator runs to connect.
.It Ic vpn-disconnect Ar vpn_gateway
Shorthand for
.Ic delete-sa
that tears down every SA associated with
.Ar vpn_gateway .
This is the command a roadwarrior client operator runs to disconnect.
.It Ic show-event
Stream every event
.Xr racoon 8
reports (SA up/down, Phase 1/2 completion, errors) until interrupted.
Useful for watching a connection attempt live.
.It Ic logout-user Ar login
Delete every SA established on behalf of the XAuth/Hybrid-auth user
.Ar login .
Only available when
.Xr racoon 8
was built with Hybrid auth support
.Pq Fl -enable-hybrid .
.El
.Pp
Command shortcuts are available:
.Bl -tag -width XXX -compact -offset indent
.It Ic rc
.Ic reload-config
.It Ic sc
.Ic show-schedule
.It Ic ss
.Ic show-sa
.It Ic gc
.Ic get-cert
.It Ic fs
.Ic flush-sa
.It Ic ds
.Ic delete-sa
.It Ic es
.Ic establish-sa
.It Ic vc
.Ic vpn-connect
.It Ic vd
.Ic vpn-disconnect
.It Ic se
.Ic show-event
.It Ic lu
.Ic logout-user
.El
.\"
.Ss Parameter specifications
.Bl -tag -width Ds -compact
.It Ar protocol
one of
.Ic isakmp , esp , ah ,
or (for
.Ic show-sa
and
.Ic flush-sa
only)
.Ic ipsec .
.It Ar saopts
.Bl -tag -width Ds -compact
.It Ic isakmp Ar family src dst
.It Brq Ic esp | ah Ar family src/prefixlen/port dst/prefixlen/port ul_proto
.El
.It Ar family
.Ic inet
or
.Ic inet6 .
.It Ar ul_proto
one of
.Ic icmp , tcp , udp , gre ,
or
.Ic any .
.El
.\"
.Sh RETURN VALUES
The command exits with 0 on success, and non-zero on errors.
.\"
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds -compact
.It Pa /var/run/racoon/racoon.sock
default admin socket path on this project's own Debian and Arch
packaging builds (compile-time
.Va ADMINPORTDIR
derived from
.Fl -localstatedir ) .
.It Pa /var/lib/racoon/racoon.sock
default admin socket path on a vanilla upstream build with no
.Fl -localstatedir
override.
.El
.Pp
Run
.Nm
.Fl s Ar /path/to/racoon.sock
if your build uses neither.
.\"
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr ipsec 4 ,
.Xr racoon.conf 5 ,
.Xr racoon 8
.\"
.Sh HISTORY
